{% doc %}
  The size promise, computed at render — DATA-MODEL.md §7.1.

  "Every size, always" is the brand's central claim, so it is computed from
  inventory on every render and never stored. Always visible, never behind
  hover: mobile has no hover, and size availability is a purchase decision.

  ── The denominator is this product's own variant count, not five ──────
  DATA-MODEL §7.1 hard-codes 5, written when the size run was fixed at five
  canonical strings. The live catalogue does not match that: the size guide
  runs S1–S9 (0–6m to 7–8y) and the products carry three to five variants
  each. Against that data a hard 5 renders "3 of 5 sizes available" on a
  frock that was only ever made in three — a false claim on the one page
  whose job is to prevent a wrong order.

  Counting against the product's own run is true under either scheme: it
  still reads "All 5 sizes available" for a five-size design, and it stays
  honest for every other. If the five-size rule is ever enforced across the
  catalogue this needs no change.

  Renders NOTHING for a product with no variants.

  @param {object} product - the product to count
  @param {string} [class] - extra classes on the line

  @example
  {% render 'sv-size-run', product: product %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign total = product.variants.size
  assign in_stock = 0
  for v in product.variants
    if v.available
      assign in_stock = in_stock | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if total > 0 -%}
  {%- if in_stock == 0 -%}
    <p class="sv-run sv-run--out {{ class }}">
      {%- if total == 1 -%}Sold out{%- else -%}Sold out in every size{%- endif -%}
    </p>
  {%- elsif in_stock == total -%}
    <p class="sv-run sv-run--full {{ class }}">
      {%- if total == 1 -%}In stock{%- else -%}All {{ total }} sizes available{%- endif -%}
    </p>
  {%- else -%}
    <p class="sv-run sv-run--partial {{ class }}">{{ in_stock }} of {{ total }} sizes available</p>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Three states, three weights of the same line. The full state is the
     claim, so it carries the gold mark; partial is plain ink; sold out is
     the warm grey, stated without alarm. */
  [data-sv] .sv-run {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6em;
    max-width: none;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-run::before {
    content: '';
    flex: none;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--tan);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-run--partial {
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  .sv-run--partial::before {
    background: var(--grey);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-run--out {
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  .sv-run--out::before {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--grey);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
